{
  "requirement": "Evidence inputs MAY have a definition form containing exactly `definition` and `text`. `definition` MUST identify one named definition; `text` MUST contain its complete raw fenced declaration as source lines, including its phrase option and explanatory body.\n\nValidation MUST reject missing definitions and changed snapshot text, identifying the definition and showing a compact diff when available. Moving an unchanged definition within its chapter MUST NOT invalidate its snapshot. Evidence displays MUST show the definition name, current source location, and recorded text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.definitions.inputs`. The only clause with no test is the MAY clause, which imposes nothing to check.\n\n**Definition form with exactly `definition` and `text`**\n- `tests/definitions.rs#fn[definition_schema_deletion_and_literal_references_are_checked]` adds an `unexpected` field to a definition input and asserts an \"unexpected field\" error.\n- `tests/definitions.rs#fn[changed_definition_snapshots_show_a_compact_diff_and_text_is_required]` removes `text`, sets it to `[]`, and sets it to a string. Each case must produce an error from `evidence/rules.ready.json` that mentions `text`.\n\n**`definition` must identify one named definition**\n- The same test appends definition inputs named `rules.ready` (a requirement) and `rules.case` (an example). Each must produce an error that names it and says \"no matching named definition\".\n- `src/evidence.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks]` asserts `inputs[0]: rules.gone: no matching named definition` for a nonexistent name.\n\n**`text` is the complete raw fenced declaration, including the phrase option and body**\n- The helpers `declaration` and `definition` in `tests/definitions.rs` build the recorded text independently of the implementation. They take the lines from the opening `:::{definition} x` fence through the closing `:::`.\n- Validation accepts those records without errors, so it requires the complete fenced text.\n- `tests/definitions.rs#fn[cyclic_dependencies_are_required_once_and_changes_require_review]` changes `:phrase: beta` to `:phrase: new beta` and changes the body text. Each change must produce an \"input text changed\" error that names the definition. The recorded file is left unchanged.\n\n**Rejecting missing definitions and changed text, identifying the definition**\n- Deleting `md/glossary.md` in `definition_schema_deletion_and_literal_references_are_checked` must yield an error containing `glossary.a` and \"no matching named definition\".\n- The \"input text changed\" errors above all assert that they contain the definition name.\n\n**Compact diff**\n- `changed_definition_snapshots_show_a_compact_diff_and_text_is_required` asserts the diff lines exactly. They are one `- See {term}`glossary.b`.` line and one `+ See {term}`glossary.b` again.` line, with no unchanged context lines.\n\n**Moving an unchanged definition within its chapter does not invalidate the snapshot**\n- `cyclic_dependencies_are_required_once_and_changes_require_review` prepends blank lines to `md/glossary.md`. This shifts both definitions' line positions. It then asserts that validation reports no errors.\n\n**Displays show name, current source location, and recorded text**\n- `src/index.rs#mod[tests]/fn[detail_page_shows_recorded_text_locations_and_first_matching_group]` checks a definition input. It asserts the `definition rules.term` label, then the `rules.term` name with `md/rules.md:9–13`, then the recorded text `recorded term`. The text is deliberately different from the source, so the display must show the recorded text. It also asserts the ordering of these parts.\n\nI found no unresolved ambiguity and no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these assertions would accept.",
  "references": "b55f37e0df05544f95f7bea68aad31a6abff40adc5e6252b5aa3542a6897bcc5",
